  "notes": "Modified cash basis, treated as cash. Trimmed pages: 1 statement of net position, 2-3 statement of activities, 4 governmental funds balance sheet, 5 governmental funds revenues/expenditures (Total Governmental Funds column), 6-7 proprietary net position and revenues/expenses, 8 proprietary cash flows, 9-11 budget schedules (General, Special Library, CDBG), 12 combining statement of General Fund departments (only the General, Street and Police columns; the Park/Pool/Library/Housing/Total half is not in the trim), 13 proprietary fund departments (Water/Sewer/Trash). Because the departments statement is incomplete in the trim and its columns cannot tie to the fund totals, General Fund detail is taken from the p9 budget schedule (ties to 517,638 / 731,855); p12 lines are not recorded to avoid double counting. No Debt Service Fund schedule. Governmental beginning/ending are fund balances 323,453 / 109,453 (all cash and CDs); ending CDs 78,657 shown as investments for information. No transfers. Business-type = Combined System Utilities Fund, measure net position: 233,937 + 319,413 - 215,776 = 337,574; nonoperating principal and interest are recorded as disbursements as printed (total matches Statement of Activities 215,776). Proprietary cash flow statement (p8: operating 134,709; capital and related financing -31,291; investing 0; cash 200,059 to 303,477) not recorded because basis is modified cash. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds balance sheet (p4, totals equal government-wide 109,453), business-type from p1. Special Library and CDBG schedules print no expenditure total. Read pages 1-13 of 13."
